 "notes": [
  "fwd_pkg/ is the HK MLA forward package (gfx1250_mla_fwd/: marker shell hip/, generator gen/, tools/) and asmkit/ as of W-S1a: a08-1 scratch/hk_opt/r4d_fwd/s1a/s1a_86a5f691.diff and r4d_ao/a3/asmkit_86a5f691.diff applied to Primus-Turbo 86a5f691 (the forward never reached Turbo). fwd_patches/ are the later versions' changes (s1a2, s1a3, s1b, fdev2, edev1 (E1), e1d, edev2 (E2)), regenerated from the a08-1 diff chain; 04 and 06 span two versions (s1a2 -> s1b, s1b -> edev1) so each main-line rung is its parent plus one patch.",
  "Generator rungs build with gen/build.py (hkl.build \"gen\" kernels): every pin is the code object a08-1 measured (scratch/hk_opt/r4d_fwd/*/cand*/*.build.json), rebuilt byte for byte with AMD clang 862306352beb; REF rungs are the same builds' HIP reference variants (HKGEN_REF=1).",
  "X6 rungs (x6_m*, scratch/hk_opt/x6_fwd_hk/best_m2f) build from the MLA backward tree (hip/: d3590be4's include/ and idx.h). m2f is pinned (b4385721); m1a / m2e / m2fx have no recorded sha, but their rebuilt code objects' notes (resources, kernarg layout) are identical to the recorded ones; the pins here are the rebuilds'.",
  "ref_ms: a08-1 measurements (prod, 30 x 7 or 5 rounds, same-process A/B), GPU0 for s1a .. s1a3 (FlyDSL ~0.752) and GPU3 for X6 (FlyDSL ~0.778, d3590be4's non-persistent forward) and s1b .. E2 (FlyDSL b12f5953 ~0.737); orientation only."
 ],
